00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,400
Whether they can be admitted as evidence

284
00:18:52,839 --> 00:18:55,400
all require time to investigate and verify.

285
00:18:56,039 --> 00:18:57,680
But procedurally speaking,

286
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,599
the defendant retracted his confession in court.

287
00:18:59,839 --> 00:19:00,640
The judges on the collegial panel

288
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:02,640
have the right to base the trial

289
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:05,319
on the evidence submitted prior to the retraction

290
00:19:05,319 --> 00:19:05,839
and pronounce a verdict.

291
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:06,519
No.

292
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,240
I'm not condemning

293
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,400
your inadequate investigation.

294
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:11,720
I believe the real problem,

295
00:19:11,799 --> 00:19:13,400
and the one who bears direct responsibility,

296
00:19:14,039 --> 00:19:16,400
is Chief Judge Yu Songfan.

297
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:19,559
Sentenced to five years in prison.

298
00:19:20,079 --> 00:19:22,839
Whether his medical condition affected the verdict

299
00:19:23,079 --> 00:19:24,720
also needs to be taken into consideration.

300
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:26,640
From a certain perspective,

301
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:28,160
the significance of a court trial

302
00:19:28,240 --> 00:19:30,000
is to serve as the final check

303
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,039
on whether law enforcement's work

304
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:33,920
is rigorous and solid enough.

305
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,000
If, when the prosecutor

306
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,400
received this flawed evidence in court,

307
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:40,119
Yu Songfan hadn't rushed to close the case

308
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:41,799
and immediately admitted it,

309
00:19:42,079 --> 00:19:43,400
but instead remained neutral,

310
00:19:43,519 --> 00:19:44,440
set aside prejudice,

311
00:19:44,599 --> 00:19:46,799
and agreed to give us time to thoroughly investigate,

312
00:19:48,440 --> 00:19:50,279
I believe the current verdict

313
00:19:50,279 --> 00:19:51,559
would be far more convincing.

314
00:19:52,079 --> 00:19:53,640
Members of the Adjudication Committee,

315
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,400
if in a case,

316
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:57,200
a lawyer is forced to become a detective,

317
00:19:57,480 --> 00:20:00,319
delving not into litigation matters,

318
00:20:00,599 --> 00:20:02,079
but rather replacing investigators

319
00:20:02,079 --> 00:20:04,160
to uncover basic criminal facts,

320
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,839
that doesn't show how capable the lawyer is,

321
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:08,279
but rather that the relevant departments

322
00:20:08,279 --> 00:20:09,720
made omissions

323
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:10,880
in handling this case.

324
00:20:12,599 --> 00:20:15,200
A true lawyer is like a fire,

325
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,359
daring to defend the marginalized,

326
00:20:17,359 --> 00:20:19,160
and daring to speak for the silenced.

327
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:21,920
We must use the light of the law

328
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:23,839
to safeguard the warmth of humanity.

329
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:28,640
Morning, Mr. Yu.

330
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,559
Hello. Morning.

331
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:34,240
Hello.

332
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:36,279
Old Yu, oh, Old Yu.

333
00:20:36,279 --> 00:20:38,480
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

334
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:39,240
Tell you what?

335
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:41,839
That you have Alzheimer's.

336
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:50,880
I'm at the door.

337
00:20:53,240 --> 00:20:54,000
See you in a bit.

338
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:00,640
The Municipal Political and Legal Affairs Commission

339
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,880
received public reports that Judge Yu Songfan

340
00:21:03,039 --> 00:21:05,559
is concealing his Alzheimer's diagnosis.

341
00:21:05,960 --> 00:21:07,039
They immediately joined the Supervision Office

342
00:21:07,039 --> 00:21:08,519
and formed a special investigation team.

343
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,799
We are investigators from the task force.

344
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:14,480
We need to ask about Yu Songfan's situation.

345
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:15,759
That's impossible.

346
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,279
That's absolutely impossible.

347
00:21:17,319 --> 00:21:18,440
Dementia?

348
00:21:18,599 --> 00:21:19,759
Mr. Yu?

349
00:21:20,359 --> 00:21:21,400
He's an absolute veteran.

350
00:21:21,599 --> 00:21:22,839
He's such a reliable guy.

351
00:21:24,759 --> 00:21:26,400
Titles like "Outstanding Grassroots Judge"...

352
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:27,559
let's not even mention those.

353
00:21:27,799 --> 00:21:29,799
He's an Outstanding Individual of the provincial courts.

354
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,519
He's been awarded personal Third-Class Merit twice.

355
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:34,319
Ask him about any law,

356
00:21:34,519 --> 00:21:35,640
and he'll tell you its origin,

357
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:36,440
the year it was amended,

358
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:37,599
and what kind of cases it applies to.

359
00:21:37,599 --> 00:21:40,599
He's a living encyclopedia of New China's judicial history.

360
00:21:40,759 --> 00:21:41,880
Do you know why Lao Yu

361
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:43,720
loves working overtime so much?

362
00:21:45,839 --> 00:21:47,000
His wife and son

363
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
were killed by criminals in a crash.

364
00:21:50,079 --> 00:21:51,960
For nine whole years since then,

365
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:54,079
work has been his entire life.

366
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:57,640
If you're going to take that away from him too...

367
00:21:58,079 --> 00:21:59,519
The current situation is that,

368
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:02,319
after consultations with experts and doctors,

369
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:03,759
it hasn't been officially confirmed

370
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:07,279
whether Yu Songfan is in the early stages of dementia

371
00:22:07,279 --> 00:22:09,119
or if it's severe depression

372
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,400
causing his psychological condition.

373
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,640
In that case, procedurally speaking,

374
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:17,160
Mr. Yu hasn't done anything wrong.

375
00:22:17,839 --> 00:22:19,519
It's too early to draw that conclusion.

376
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:21,079
But as of now,

377
00:22:21,599 --> 00:22:23,400
his actions are at most a breach of regulations.

378
00:22:24,319 --> 00:22:25,319
We are only temporarily suspending

379
00:22:25,319 --> 00:22:26,920
all of his trial duties.

380
00:22:27,640 --> 00:22:30,359
The final decision depends on further investigation.

381
00:23:02,079 --> 00:23:02,799
Thank you.

382
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:03,920
Hello.

383
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:05,759
I'd like to apply for enforcement on this case.

384
00:23:20,599 --> 00:23:22,079
This case hasn't taken effect yet.

385
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:23,920
That's impossible.

386
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:26,480
It's been effective for at least five days.

387
00:23:26,559 --> 00:23:27,559
What do you mean, "impossible"?

388
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:28,799
Go and ask

389
00:23:28,799 --> 00:23:30,359
the presiding judge of this case yourself.

390
00:23:30,599 --> 00:23:32,359
It doesn't show up on my computer.

391
00:23:33,079 --> 00:23:33,920
Next.

392
00:23:41,759 --> 00:23:42,920
Hello, Judge Sun.

393
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:44,119
Hi, it's Ding Ning.

394
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,480
Regarding our application for enforcement,

395
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:47,759
have you confirmed it?

396
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:49,319
I'm at the filing division now, and they...

397
00:23:49,559 --> 00:23:50,960
Sorry, Lawyer Ding.

398
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:52,839
I forgot to click confirm in the system.

399
00:23:52,960 --> 00:23:53,720
You forgot?

400
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:54,880
Yes, I forgot.

401
00:23:55,839 --> 00:23:57,319
Maybe I'm getting Alzheimer's too.

402
00:23:58,039 --> 00:23:58,799
Could I trouble you

403
00:23:58,799 --> 00:24:00,880
to click confirm with your mouse now?

404
00:24:01,079 --> 00:24:02,680
I'm in a hurry to get this processed.

405
00:24:03,279 --> 00:24:04,200
Is that all?

406
00:24:04,599 --> 00:24:06,640
I thought you'd write another report letter

407
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:08,200
to Trial Supervision and the Political-Legal Commission.

408
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:10,279
Your law firm is familiar with the process anyway.

409
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:11,400
What did you say?

410
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,440
Sorry.

411
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:13,599
I'm running errands outside right now.

412
00:24:13,599 --> 00:24:14,720
I'll confirm it when I get back.

413
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:15,759
Sorry. Gotta go.

414
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:17,759
Hello?

415
00:24:24,799 --> 00:24:26,119
It was just an internal investigation.

416
00:24:26,119 --> 00:24:27,599
Nothing actually happened.

417
00:24:27,839 --> 00:24:29,640
Yet you submitted your resignation.

418
00:24:30,039 --> 00:24:32,240
Doesn't that just validate their false accusations?

419
00:24:32,799 --> 00:24:33,480
It's fine.

420
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:36,759
It's heavy, be careful.

421
00:24:39,799 --> 00:24:41,319
I'll load these onto the car first, then.

422
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:43,079
Alright, thanks for your help.

423
00:25:13,319 --> 00:25:14,119
Sorry about that.

424
00:25:17,359 --> 00:25:18,119
Thanks.

425
00:25:18,319 --> 00:25:19,160
Don't help her.

426
00:25:19,759 --> 00:25:21,960
She's Ding Ning, the one who reported Mr. Yu.

427
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,440
I'm sorry.

428
00:25:37,599 --> 00:25:40,039
Actually, you didn't do anything wrong.

429
00:25:40,799 --> 00:25:42,119
They weren't targeting you.

430
00:25:42,839 --> 00:25:44,440
Or even me.

431
00:25:45,519 --> 00:25:48,880
It's just that everyone's having a hard time.

432
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:52,799
Don't take it personally.

433
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:55,720
Thank you.

434
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:13,039
Let me.

435
00:26:15,759 --> 00:26:16,720
Thank you. Thank you.

436
00:26:18,039 --> 00:26:19,240
Take Lao Yu home first.

437
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:19,640
Okay.

438
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:21,079
No, no. Let's handle our business first.

439
00:26:21,279 --> 00:26:22,680
Stop arguing. Let's just do it this way.

440
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:24,160
Quick, quick, quick.

441
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:25,160
Mr. Yu.

442
00:26:25,839 --> 00:26:26,880
Here. Goodbye.

443
00:26:28,839 --> 00:26:30,359
Okay, okay. Sorry for the trouble.

444
00:26:30,359 --> 00:26:31,000
Thank you.

445
00:26:31,079 --> 00:26:31,759
See you.

446
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:36,960
The media really wants to get a shot later

447
00:26:36,960 --> 00:26:38,400
of us delivering the verdict,

448
00:26:38,400 --> 00:26:39,440
to capture the family's reaction.

449
00:26:39,759 --> 00:26:41,039
It'll also promote legal awareness.

450
00:26:41,319 --> 00:26:42,160
As for the interview script,

451
00:26:42,160 --> 00:26:43,240
I've already gone over it.

452
00:26:43,240 --> 00:26:44,000
There shouldn't be any issues.

453
00:26:44,119 --> 00:26:45,960
Does this schedule for later work for you?

454
00:26:52,319 --> 00:26:53,559
The Pingcun intentional homicide case,

455
00:26:53,559 --> 00:26:54,880
after a year and a half of trial,

456
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:56,240
has finally seen justice served.

457
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:57,039
Our whole family has been waiting.

458
00:26:57,039 --> 00:26:59,920
Thank you, honorable judges of the district court!

459
00:27:00,119 --> 00:27:01,400
Their names are cleared,

460
00:27:01,519 --> 00:27:02,279
but what about you?

461
00:27:03,720 --> 00:27:04,640
Don't you feel wronged?

462
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:10,240
Even I feel wronged for you.

463
00:27:12,359 --> 00:27:14,400
Why do you always act like everything is fine?

464
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:17,279
All these years, I've wanted to make it up to you,

465
00:27:19,200 --> 00:27:20,920
but I just don't know how.

466
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:25,359
I owe you two lives.

467
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:27,839
This matter

468
00:27:28,839 --> 00:27:30,759
has weighed heavily on my mind for years.

469
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,079
And now you've run into this mess again.

470
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:39,400
Why does all the suffering fall on one person?

471
00:27:43,680 --> 00:27:44,279
All right, all right.

472
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:47,799
Don't cry. Don't cry.

473
00:27:49,519 --> 00:27:50,720
Justice has been served.

474
00:27:50,720 --> 00:27:51,839
The presiding judge of this case,

475
00:27:51,839 --> 00:27:53,839
Judge Gu of the Fulin District People's Court,

476
00:27:53,839 --> 00:27:55,720
came in person to deliver the verdict.

477
00:29:00,279 --> 00:29:01,759
Dad, do you know

478
00:29:01,759 --> 00:29:03,480
that cicadas lie dormant underground for 12 years,

479
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:06,640
only emerging to molt in their 13th year?

480
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:07,519
Do you know why that is?

481
00:29:07,920 --> 00:29:09,839
It's because their natural predators

482
00:29:09,839 --> 00:29:13,039
appear in massive numbers during certain years.

483
00:29:13,039 --> 00:29:15,319
They use the prime number principle to find a safe cycle.

484
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:17,279
By this calculation,

485
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:18,880
the 13th year, being a prime number,

486
00:29:19,359 --> 00:29:20,640
is when they're least likely to encounter predators.

487
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:33,319
As for the logic to solve this problem,

488
00:29:33,319 --> 00:29:35,480
I'm actually still not entirely clear on it.

489
00:29:35,960 --> 00:29:39,119
DE is parallel to AB.

490
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:42,000
And DE equals half of AB.

491
00:29:42,359 --> 00:29:43,279
That makes sense.

492
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:45,759
Then OF is parallel to AB.

493
00:29:46,039 --> 00:29:48,960
And OF also equals half of AB.

494
00:29:49,240 --> 00:29:50,559
So DE equals...

495
00:29:53,119 --> 00:29:53,720
OF.

496
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:54,599
Right.

497
00:29:55,039 --> 00:29:58,039
Dad, I won another award in the Math Olympiad!

498
00:30:10,880 --> 00:30:12,200
Yu Xiaoyue, what are you doing?

499
00:30:12,359 --> 00:30:14,160
Yu Xiaoyue, I'm your teacher!

500
00:30:14,279 --> 00:30:16,200
Are you crazy? What are you doing?

501
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:19,079
What are you doing?

502
00:30:19,599 --> 00:30:21,400
Yu Xiaoyue, what are you doing?

503
00:30:21,400 --> 00:30:22,720
I'm your teacher!

504
00:30:27,039 --> 00:30:28,160
What are you doing?

505
00:31:02,759 --> 00:31:06,160
It's really hard to move on from the past.

506
00:31:08,599 --> 00:31:10,400
But you still need to keep moving forward.

507
00:31:11,359 --> 00:31:13,599
Yeah, a lot of people say that.

508
00:31:13,599 --> 00:31:14,480
Move forward.

509
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:19,000
But at my age, moving forward

510
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,720
just means reuniting with my family.

511
00:31:23,160 --> 00:31:24,880
Dad, come eat.

512
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:27,400
I made your favorite braised pig ears.

513
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:31,200
In the end, who doesn't

514
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:33,759
end up all alone?

515
00:31:35,839 --> 00:31:38,799
I just reached that point a bit early.

516
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:41,200
I'm thinking

517
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:46,079
I shouldn't burden anyone else anymore.

518
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:49,079
Besides,

519
00:31:50,799 --> 00:31:53,240
it's not about whether I have hope.

520
00:31:54,640 --> 00:31:59,480
It's that I don't want any hope at all.

521
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:05,279
Do you understand?

522
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:16,440
The paperwork at Rongshan is almost done.

523
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:18,079
Right now,

524
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:19,960
we only have one obstacle left.

525
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:22,319
The kid's father absolutely refuses to let go.

526
00:32:24,160 --> 00:32:25,000
That Old Kang...

527
00:32:26,759 --> 00:32:29,519
No one around there can handle him.

528
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:34,279
Okay, I'll figure something out.

529
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:36,920
Here's what you asked for.

530
00:32:38,799 --> 00:32:40,599
The prosecutors are refusing to let go.

531
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:42,000
If they keep

532
00:32:42,000 --> 00:32:44,400
digging into the Fuxia Group lead,

533
00:32:44,440 --> 00:32:45,960
they'll track us down very soon.

534
00:32:53,319 --> 00:32:55,359
How are things on your end?

535
00:32:58,160 --> 00:32:59,200
Going pretty smoothly.

536
00:33:02,759 --> 00:33:04,240
Do you really think

537
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:07,200
we can make him listen to us?

538
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:08,759
Some people

539
00:33:09,319 --> 00:33:10,839
seem invulnerable

540
00:33:12,039 --> 00:33:13,559
because they have nothing to lose.

541
00:33:15,039 --> 00:33:16,680
But the less they have to lose,

542
00:33:17,799 --> 00:33:19,680
the harder it is for them to resist

543
00:33:20,160 --> 00:33:22,279
even a sliver of hope.

544
00:33:41,079 --> 00:33:41,799
Boss

545
00:33:53,680 --> 00:33:54,319
Boss.

546
00:33:54,799 --> 00:33:55,359
What is it?

547
00:33:57,119 --> 00:33:58,039
Are you okay?

548
00:33:59,119 --> 00:33:59,920
I'm fine.

549
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:01,599
What's the matter?

550
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:02,720
What's the matter?

551
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:04,440
I've been calling you all afternoon.

552
00:34:04,440 --> 00:34:05,240
Why didn't you answer?

553
00:34:06,759 --> 00:34:08,440
Good thing I have your spare key.

554
00:34:08,599 --> 00:34:10,400
Otherwise, no one would know if you died in here today.

555
00:34:10,400 --> 00:34:11,440
What are you doing at home?

556
00:34:12,920 --> 00:34:13,719
Burning things.

557
00:34:13,800 --> 00:34:14,519
Burning what?

558
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:15,559
Because...

559
00:34:16,440 --> 00:34:17,840
a judge who has resigned

560
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:21,360
shouldn't keep certain court documents anymore.

561
00:34:22,079 --> 00:34:23,280
It's my responsibility.

562
00:34:24,159 --> 00:34:25,119
What's wrong with that?

563
00:34:31,239 --> 00:34:32,400
Burning documents.

564
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:34,719
What are you doing?

565
00:34:35,719 --> 00:34:36,800
Look closely, everyone.

566
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:38,800
This little old man...

567
00:34:39,320 --> 00:34:40,599
I looked for him all afternoon.

568
00:34:41,400 --> 00:34:43,079
He tells me he's home burning documents.

569
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:47,320
Just to be clear...

570
00:34:47,840 --> 00:34:51,960
he's not committing suicide by burning charcoal.

571
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:53,119
Ma Tingting, you...

572
00:34:55,119 --> 00:34:57,639
I hope everyone who sees this video...

573
00:34:57,639 --> 00:34:59,440
who has nothing to do in the afternoon...

574
00:34:59,440 --> 00:35:01,079
comes over to help him burn documents.

575
00:35:01,079 --> 00:35:02,440
Hey, are you done?

576
00:35:02,719 --> 00:35:04,519
Delete that. Don't post it.

577
00:35:09,840 --> 00:35:11,159
Look at my job.

578
00:35:11,599 --> 00:35:12,320
The pay is low.

579
00:35:12,679 --> 00:35:13,639
The workload is heavy.

580
00:35:13,639 --> 00:35:14,800
And I have to work overtime every day.

581
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:16,480
From the start, I said I wouldn't come.

582
00:35:16,480 --> 00:35:17,960
I didn't want this job.

583
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:19,480
It makes me look like an old lady all day.

584
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:20,360
I can't even get my nails done.

585
00:35:20,360 --> 00:35:21,960
I can't even dye my hair if I want to.

586
00:35:22,199 --> 00:35:23,480
That Xiao Sun...

587
00:35:23,480 --> 00:35:24,840
kisses ass every day.

588
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:26,000
He doesn't do any work.

589
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:27,760
No wonder he never makes mistakes.

590
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:29,519
I've figured it out.

591
00:35:29,760 --> 00:35:30,800
Now that you're leaving...

592
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:33,079
what hope do I have for the future?

593
00:35:33,079 --> 00:35:33,880
None at all.

594
00:35:35,679 --> 00:35:37,079
I'm so frustrated.

595
00:35:37,079 --> 00:35:38,440
I'm not as calm as you are.

596
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:40,039
I want to keep moving up.

597
00:35:40,239 --> 00:35:41,559
But I have no connections up there.

598
00:35:41,599 --> 00:35:42,880
I'll just be stuck as a judge.

599
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:44,199
I've had enough.

600
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:45,599
I'm depressed, you know?

601
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:48,239
Hey, Old Yu. Seriously.

602
00:35:48,519 --> 00:35:49,639
I'm very depressed.

603
00:35:49,719 --> 00:35:51,360
You need to listen to me very carefully.

604
00:35:52,519 --> 00:35:55,320
Judge Chen is 55 or 56.

605
00:35:55,599 --> 00:35:56,840
He's about to retire.

606
00:35:57,039 --> 00:35:58,360
You know how old his wife is?

607
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:01,159
His wife is almost 20 years younger than him.

608
00:36:01,360 --> 00:36:03,320
They went to get IVF.

609
00:36:03,519 --> 00:36:06,079
Turns out, Judge Chen has a problem.

610
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:08,239
They finally managed to conceive.

611
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:10,159
From conceiving to finally giving birth...

612
00:36:10,159 --> 00:36:11,039
Guess what?

613
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:17,440
It wasn't theirs.

614
00:36:17,440 --> 00:36:18,480
The hospital made a mistake.

615
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:19,760
Medical malpractice.

616
00:36:20,599 --> 00:36:22,000
After all that, it wasn't even his.

617
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:23,920
It cracks me up.

618
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:28,440
The environment at home right now...

619
00:36:29,440 --> 00:36:30,440
You know, it's just...

620
00:36:31,039 --> 00:36:33,440
Unusually cold.

621
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,599
I don't know if I should get a divorce.

622
00:36:38,679 --> 00:36:39,800
I'm just worried that...

623
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:41,559
a divorce might be bad for the child.

624
00:36:41,559 --> 00:36:43,360
But if I don't get a divorce now...

625
00:36:43,360 --> 00:36:45,280
and just keep settling for this...

626
00:36:46,039 --> 00:36:47,519
Do you have any good advice?

627
00:36:49,039 --> 00:36:50,920
My wife and son are dead.

628
00:36:56,440 --> 00:36:57,159
Brother.

629
00:36:57,679 --> 00:36:59,119
Calling you highly respected

630
00:36:59,119 --> 00:37:00,519
is certainly no exaggeration.

631
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:01,760
How many years does it take

632
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:03,760
to produce a great judge like you?

633
00:37:03,960 --> 00:37:05,559
It's no stretch to say your protégés are everywhere.

634
00:37:05,559 --> 00:37:07,639
You obviously could've taken medical retirement,

635
00:37:07,639 --> 00:37:11,000
but you insisted on resigning instead.

636
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:12,679
Then... then how are you going to get by?

637
00:37:13,920 --> 00:37:16,320
I'm just genuinely worried about your livelihood.

638
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:17,719
I just hope that from now on,

639
00:37:17,719 --> 00:37:18,719
you'll be financially secure.

640
00:37:18,760 --> 00:37:19,559
Of course, how should I put this...

641
00:37:19,559 --> 00:37:20,440
regarding this matter...

642
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:21,719
what I really want is

643
00:37:21,719 --> 00:37:23,400
for you to talk to that Judge Li,

644
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:27,199
so he learns the meaning of fairness and justice.

645
00:37:30,880 --> 00:37:31,480
Right.

646
00:37:45,519 --> 00:37:46,239
Senior.

647
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:50,039
How about that?

648
00:37:55,199 --> 00:37:55,960
Am I right?

649
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:58,159
I told you we'd get a retrial.

650
00:37:58,159 --> 00:37:58,599
Alright, alright.

651
00:37:58,599 --> 00:37:59,320
He said you couldn't do it.

652
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:01,199
So we have a shot at overturning the case now?

653
00:38:01,199 --> 00:38:02,159
Absolutely.

654
00:38:02,159 --> 00:38:03,320
We'll overturn it for sure.

655
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:04,559
See?

656
00:38:04,559 --> 00:38:05,320
You're buying dinner. You lost the bet.

657
00:38:05,480 --> 00:38:06,239
No problem.

658
00:38:06,320 --> 00:38:07,880
Hunan cuisine tonight, my treat.

659
00:38:07,880 --> 00:38:08,280
How does that sound?

660
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:09,239
In that case, we're all going.

661
00:38:09,239 --> 00:38:10,239
Let's all go! Everyone!

662
00:38:10,239 --> 00:38:11,280
Good job, Ding Ning.

663
00:38:11,559 --> 00:38:12,599
You won me a free dinner.

664
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:16,360
This is going to be a classic case.

665
00:38:27,679 --> 00:38:28,519
I'm sorry.

666
00:38:28,880 --> 00:38:31,320
Actually, you did nothing wrong.

667
00:38:32,199 --> 00:38:35,599
It's just that everyone's having a hard time.

668
00:38:38,159 --> 00:38:39,559
You're thinking about Yu Songfan, aren't you?

669
00:38:40,599 --> 00:38:43,159
Thinking you might've ruined a good judge.

670
00:38:45,679 --> 00:38:47,519
I heard that when he was young,

671
00:38:47,800 --> 00:38:49,480
he received a provincial commendation.

672
00:38:49,679 --> 00:38:52,000
Someone was apparently framed for kidnapping.

673
00:38:52,320 --> 00:38:53,840
In the end, Yu Songfan took charge,

674
00:38:53,840 --> 00:38:55,440
found out he was innocent,

675
00:38:55,639 --> 00:38:56,519
acquitted him,

676
00:38:56,719 --> 00:38:57,719
and let him go.

677
00:38:58,519 --> 00:38:59,519
There's a saying.

678
00:38:59,639 --> 00:39:02,440
"Crime only pollutes the stream,

679
00:39:03,119 --> 00:39:05,000
while an unjust judgment

680
00:39:05,280 --> 00:39:06,920
pollutes the source."

681
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:15,920
Boss, what will happen to Yu Songfan?

682
00:39:16,119 --> 00:39:17,679
I wouldn't call it a punishment.

683
00:39:17,679 --> 00:39:19,320
He submitted his resignation himself,

684
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:20,880
and the district court has approved it.

685
00:39:20,880 --> 00:39:21,679
Then will he really,

686
00:39:21,679 --> 00:39:23,400
like those people online say,

687
00:39:23,400 --> 00:39:25,679
be harassed by his former litigants

688
00:39:25,679 --> 00:39:27,559
and their families?

689
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:29,119
Who can say for sure?

690
00:39:43,880 --> 00:39:44,599
What is it?

691
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:46,480
I've been here since after 5 a.m.

692
00:39:46,840 --> 00:39:48,679
Figured I'd see if I could bump into you.

693
00:39:49,239 --> 00:39:50,920
If not, I'd just head to work when it's time.

694
00:39:52,039 --> 00:39:52,880
Thanks.

695
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:54,840
How did you know

696
00:39:54,840 --> 00:39:56,440
I jog here in the morning?

697
00:39:57,480 --> 00:39:59,199
Not many people run in leather shoes.

698
00:39:59,719 --> 00:40:02,159
Are you still not over it,

699
00:40:02,800 --> 00:40:03,960
so you corner me here

700
00:40:03,960 --> 00:40:05,960
to push me in when I'm not looking,

701
00:40:05,960 --> 00:40:06,679
to make me drown,

702
00:40:06,679 --> 00:40:08,400
and die? Is that it?

703
00:40:13,039 --> 00:40:14,440
What's wrong? Why are you looking for me?

704
00:40:14,760 --> 00:40:16,519
I... I heard

705
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:17,719
that years ago,

706
00:40:17,719 --> 00:40:19,559
you helped clear a kidnapping suspect's name.

707
00:40:20,719 --> 00:40:22,639
The Zhang Wenming case, right?

708
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:26,480
Actually, when I first became a lawyer,

709
00:40:26,480 --> 00:40:27,360
whenever I helped

710
00:40:27,360 --> 00:40:29,039
an innocent client,

711
00:40:30,079 --> 00:40:31,559
I'd feel a little better.

712
00:40:33,760 --> 00:40:35,440
So no matter what mistakes

713
00:40:36,760 --> 00:40:38,159
a person makes,

714
00:40:38,159 --> 00:40:39,519
even if he is a criminal,

715
00:40:39,519 --> 00:40:40,679
his...

716
00:40:41,199 --> 00:40:42,199
his life

717
00:40:42,199 --> 00:40:44,159
is always important to someone.

718
00:40:44,159 --> 00:40:46,039
Like his daughter,

719
00:40:46,199 --> 00:40:47,320
and his family.

720
00:40:48,360 --> 00:40:49,239
My dad...

721
00:40:52,199 --> 00:40:53,239
My dad was convicted of

722
00:40:53,239 --> 00:40:54,840
kidnapping a child resulting in death,

723
00:40:55,039 --> 00:40:55,800
and was executed for it.

724
00:40:57,800 --> 00:40:58,760
Maybe it was for

725
00:40:58,760 --> 00:41:00,440
that little obsession in my heart.

726
00:41:01,800 --> 00:41:03,519
I stand at the defense table time and again,

727
00:41:04,119 --> 00:41:06,039
just to change how it ended back then.

728
00:41:10,480 --> 00:41:12,920
So don't take my resignation to heart.

729
00:41:14,519 --> 00:41:16,599
Aren't you all still on this path?

730
00:41:17,480 --> 00:41:18,880
People will always leave,

731
00:41:18,880 --> 00:41:20,559
but there will always be someone to remember them.

732
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:21,960
And that's enough.

733
00:42:01,280 --> 00:42:02,159
Hello.

734
00:42:02,760 --> 00:42:03,559
It's me.

735
00:42:04,519 --> 00:42:05,880
Now that you've resigned,

736
00:42:06,599 --> 00:42:08,400
I must disappear for a while

737
00:42:08,440 --> 00:42:10,000
to handle some things.

738
00:42:10,719 --> 00:42:11,840
But I promise you,

739
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:13,519
as soon as I get back,

740
00:42:13,880 --> 00:42:15,400
we'll meet up.

741
00:42:17,559 --> 00:42:18,760
Of course,

742
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:19,960
right now, are you

743
00:42:19,960 --> 00:42:22,400
still dying to see my face?

744
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:25,480
Alright.

745
00:42:26,199 --> 00:42:27,679
Let me adjust the camera.

746
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:35,119
Ding Ning.

747
00:42:35,639 --> 00:42:36,679
Recognize me?
